## Admin tab visibility and Sandbox resume (v1.19.8 — mandatory)
- Apply Admin-only Debug tab visibility after the general account gate updates tab styles, and after authentication initialization. A signed-in Admin must not need to click another tab to refresh Debug visibility; non-Admin accounts must never see or access it.
- On refresh, always verify the Supabase session before resuming a Sandbox. If same-tab sessionStorage contains a valid Sandbox snapshot whose username exactly matches authenticated Admin, restore its temporary state and live-state backup before releasing the startup gate; do not wait on cloud-save hydration unnecessarily.
- Sandbox resume must never bypass authentication, never run for non-Admin/mismatched snapshots, and never write temporary Sandbox state to the real account. Missing/malformed snapshots fall back to normal cloud restoration.
- Update changelog, service-worker cache namespace, and Debug report versions together. Verify Admin/non-Admin tab visibility, Sandbox refresh resume, and live-account isolation in a browser.

## Admin identity restoration and Bloodthirst reward labels (v1.19.7 — mandatory)
- After refresh, recover the username from Supabase metadata first. If absent, reuse `wayfarer-last-username` only when `usernameEmail(candidate)` exactly matches the authenticated Supabase email; never grant Admin based only on an unrelated global cached username or email local-part guess. Re-render Debug visibility after auth restoration.
- Quest reward UI must display both the locked-in theme bonus XP and theme bonus gold when present. Keep total quest rewards and all other bonus labels intact.
- Update changelog, service-worker cache namespace, and Debug report version strings together.

## Admin Debug Sandbox persistence after auth bootstrap (v1.19.6 — mandatory)
- Restore a saved same-tab Debug Sandbox only after Supabase has identified the signed-in Admin account. The Debug script must handle either ordering: authentication may resolve before or after `debug.js` loads.
- Never gate restoration on the absence of `cloudUser`; that skips restoration for the normal signed-in Admin case. Dispatch/listen for an auth-restored event and keep restoration idempotent.
- Restore only when the stored snapshot username exactly matches the authenticated username. Do not clear a valid snapshot just because authentication is not ready yet. Keep the real account save isolated from the temporary Sandbox.
- Update changelog, service-worker cache version, and Debug report version strings together. Verify Sandbox persistence across a real same-tab refresh without altering live account progress.

## Index-level authentication bootstrap (v1.19.5 — mandatory)
- Create the Supabase client and begin persisted-session restoration in `index.html` before loading modular application scripts.
- `core-account.js` must reuse the exact `window.wayfarerSupabaseClient` and `window.wayfarerAuthPreflight` promise; do not create a competing client or race a second initial `getSession()` call when preflight exists.
- Keep session persistence enabled with localStorage. A confirmed null session releases the gate to login; timeout/errors preserve local progress and must not be interpreted as sign-out.
- Keep bounded timeouts and the independent watchdog. Verify signed-in hard refresh, signed-out startup, and cloud-save loading in a real browser before declaring the issue fixed.

## Independent startup watchdog (v1.19.4 — mandatory)
- Keep an independent page-level watchdog in index.html in addition to Supabase promise timeouts. It must reveal a retryable recovery state if modular startup stalls or fails before registering its own timeout.
- On watchdog recovery, preserve the device copy and never overwrite cloud data automatically. If the authenticated user is already identified, render the retained local copy with a clear cloud-recovery status; otherwise show the normal sign-in path.
- Update service-worker cache version, changelog, and Debug version strings together. A release is not considered fixed until signed-in refresh is verified in a real browser.

## Bounded authentication startup recovery (v1.19.3 — mandatory)
- Neither Supabase session restoration nor cloud-save hydration may hold the startup gate indefinitely. Wrap each startup network operation in a bounded timeout and release the gate into a retryable recovery state on timeout.
- A timeout is not proof that the user is signed out. Preserve the device copy and never reset account state because auth or cloud reads are slow/unavailable.
- If `getSession()` definitively resolves with no session, release the gate to the normal login screen. If session restoration times out, show a recoverable status and permit sign-in retry.
- Keep background sync outside the critical path after account state is restored. Verify both signed-in and signed-out refresh paths in a real browser before claiming the issue fixed.

## Bloodthirst character artwork mapping (v1.19.2 — mandatory)
- Keep `male-bloodthirst.webp` mapped to the intended male artwork and `female-bloodthirst.webp` mapped to the intended female artwork. Existing runtime references use these filenames; when correcting artwork assignments, verify the actual image contents, not just the filename strings.

## Debug Sandbox-only actions (v1.19.1 — mandatory)
- No Debug option may mutate live account state. All Debug controls, including resource grants/removals, character reset/restore, cooldown reset, gender tests, fault injection, inspection, and test runners, require the exact Admin account and an active isolated Sandbox. Only Start Sandbox is available outside Sandbox; Exit Sandbox is available only while active.
- Enforce Sandbox access in individual event handlers and with the central capture-phase interaction guard. Render-time disabled controls are supplemental only, never the sole protection.
- Character reset snapshots are sandbox-scoped and stored in sessionStorage, never in the live account's localStorage. Reset/restore cannot overwrite or restore a live-account snapshot.
- UI descriptions must never imply that Debug grants or recovery controls work in live mode. Any new Debug control must default disabled until Sandbox is active.

## Authentication startup gate (v1.19.0 — mandatory)
- Keep the application behind a visible loading gate until `getSession()` has definitively resolved. Do not expose the login screen, call the user signed out, or render account-specific content while auth restoration is pending.
- If a session exists, restore the matching account's cloud save (or preserve its local copy if the cloud read fails) before releasing the gate. Treat transient null auth callbacks as non-authoritative until initial restoration completes.
- Unexpected restoration exceptions must release the gate with a retryable status, preserve local progress, and reset hydration flags safely. Never silently reset an account because startup failed.
- Background cloud sync must not block app readiness after account state has been restored. Test hard refresh and browser restart with a real signed-in session before claiming the issue fixed.

## Debug Sandbox hard boundary and auth restoration (v1.18.9 — mandatory)
- Every Debug control that changes gameplay, account state, progression, inventory, equipment, dates, cooldowns, feature flags, fault injection, or test fixtures must be blocked unless the exact Admin account is signed in and Sandbox is active. The only outside-Sandbox action allowed is entering Sandbox; leaving Sandbox is allowed only while active.
- Enforce this both in each action handler and with a central capture-phase interaction guard. Do not rely on hidden/disabled UI alone. Do not let resource grants, removals, character reset/restore, cooldown reset, gender changes, unlock-all, or fault injection touch live state.
- Sandbox changes must never persist into the real account or shared local save. Reset/restore snapshots must be sandbox-scoped and must not overwrite a live-account snapshot.
- On startup, Supabase getSession() is authoritative for session restoration. Ignore transient null auth callbacks until initial restoration completes; do not clear username/session UI due to an early callback. Preserve account data if restoration fails and show a retryable status. Verify page refresh, sign-in/out, and account isolation in a browser before claiming success.

